\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{A scalar test of a transport}
\date{2026-11-19}

\p{At one end of an edge, send the scalar along the link. At the
other, take its inner product with the scalar already there. This
measurement detects agreement of two signs. On a circle it detects
the cosine of the angle between the vectors. Can it also tell
clockwise rotation from counterclockwise rotation? The
[group element in scalar frames](fdip-010X) retains the direction
of rotation before the pairing is taken.}
